sequenceDiagram
    participant User as User Browser
    participant Route as OpenShift Route<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant OAuth as OAuth Proxy Sidecar<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS
    participant JL as JupyterLab / code-server<br/>8888/TCP or 8080/TCP HTTP
    participant S3 as S3-Compatible Storage<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant Git as Git Repository<br/>443/TCP HTTPS

    Note over User,JL: Flow 1: User Workbench Access

    User->>Route: HTTPS/443<br/>OpenShift OAuth
    Route->>OAuth: TLS/8443<br/>OAuth Token validation
    OAuth->>JL: HTTP/8888 (Jupyter) or 8080 (CodeServer)<br/>Pod-internal, no auth
    JL-->>OAuth: Response
    OAuth-->>Route: Response
    Route-->>User: HTTPS Response

    Note over JL,S3: Data Access from Workbench

    JL->>S3: HTTPS/443<br/>boto3 SDK<br/>AWS IAM / Access Key
    S3-->>JL: Data objects

    JL->>Git: HTTPS/443<br/>git CLI
    Git-->>JL: Repository content

    Note over User,S3: Flow 2: Pipeline Runtime Execution (Elyra)

    participant KFP as Kubeflow Pipelines
    participant RT as Runtime Container<br/>(Elyra Bootstrapper)

    KFP->>RT: Launch pipeline step<br/>Service Account auth
    RT->>S3: HTTPS/443<br/>Download/upload artifacts<br/>Access Key / IAM
    S3-->>RT: Artifacts
    RT->>KFP: Report status<br/>Bearer Token
    KFP-->>RT: Acknowledged
